Description: Linux daemon for the ASUS ZenBook Duo 2024 (UX8406MA)
 zbd fills the gap between the upstream kernel/desktop stack and the
 ASUS ZenBook Duo 2024 — a laptop with two stacked OLED panels and a
 detachable Bluetooth/USB keyboard. It detects the keyboard
 transition (attached vs detached), enables or disables the second
 internal display (eDP-2) accordingly, sets per-output wallpapers,
 drives the keyboard backlight via the vendor HID protocol, caps the
 battery charge and wires the Intel Smart Sound DMIC into the
 default PulseAudio source.
 .
 Two binaries are installed:
   * /usr/sbin/zbd-system — small, hardened, oneshot service that
     applies the persistent hardware tunables (backlight, battery,
     keyboard backlight, DMIC) at boot.
   * /usr/bin/zbd-tray   — GTK tray + event monitors (Bluetooth, USB,
     iio-sensor-proxy) that runs in the user's graphical session.
 .
 The display backend is selected at runtime: xrandr on X11, gdctl on
 Wayland with GNOME (default on Ubuntu 26.04). A polkit policy and
 D-Bus interface for runtime privileged operations are planned.
